From 229dc2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:15:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Wave 1, place: Back returns to the same spot; typing and
 open sections are kept

The owner asked (2026-11-11) for a stress test of every touch and input. This is the
shell's "place" share of wave 1, fixed once for every page: Back, Forward and a reload
put back the scroll, the open sections and what was under the thumb; a save's redraw
keeps open sections, typing elsewhere, the focus and the tapped thing where it was; a
page that brings its own answer into view still wins. Typing that was not saved waits
in its boxes with a quiet "Not saved yet" and one way to undo it (never on Settings,
never a password, key or search box). A way back on screen (a[data-back]) is the
phone's Back when the page it names is just behind. A confirmation that cannot be read
where the page drew it is copied at the bottom, lets a tap through to what is under it,
carries the notice's own way on, and leaves by itself. A form left open is opened again
on Back; a one-tap change's way back (Undo, "Put back my amounts") comes back with its
page while the plan is unchanged; Settings' erase and restore forget the typing kept for
the old plan.

New: core/place.js (only core/app.js imports it), numbered history entries, layers and
ways back in core/router.js (ctx.layer, ctx.back, ctx.redraw), tests/place.test.mjs,
tests/router-replace.test.mjs. frame.js: data-back on its six way-back links.
core/ui/base.css: the note and the kept-typing lines; body { overflow-anchor: none }.
docs/CONVENTIONS.md: "What the shell keeps for you" and the three ctx rows. No view.js
changes.

Simple first (the owner's rule of 2026-11-12): a form whose typing is put back says "Not
saved yet" once beside its button and once more under the first box it put back only
when that box is far from the button, never under every box.

On the branch's newer tip (5614682): the "saved by a newer version" notice takes the
page's place, so it borrows no room and is shown from the top; Back, a reload or a
redraw far down a page would otherwise leave it off the screen.

